                    <h6>Take care of your workforce. Movement = Longevity</h6>
                    <h4>Did you know?</h4>
                    <div class="line-dec"></div>
                  </div>
                  <p>
                    According to a study by the World Health Organization,
                    sedentary behaviour is responsible for 3.2 million deaths
                    every year. Reports from national libraries of medicine
                    suggest that sedentary behaviour is a risk factor for
                    chronic diseases such as obesity, diabetes, and
                    cardiovascular diseases. Activity tracker based studies
                    found that office workers spend 77% of their working day
                    sedentary, and attained most of their PA (Physical Activity)
                    after work hours.<br />
                    <br />
                    WFH office workers spend 48% of their day engaging in
                    sedentary behavior. Further, individuals spent almost an
                    hour more with combined sleep and time in bed. According to
                    Forbes, 32.6 million people will work remote in America
                    alone. Recent survey results reported a reduction of up to
                    67% in PA and 42.6% of reported sitting for more than eight
                    hours a day.
                  </p>
